# Hosts a user browser may NOT reach, one POSIX extended regex per line.
#
# `FilterDefaultDeny No` in tinyproxy.conf: everything not listed passes. What
# is listed is the inside of the deployment — our own containers by name and
# by private address — and the cloud metadata range. Chromium is started with
# `--proxy-bypass-list="<-loopback>"`, so even loopback goes through here.

^engenty-
^localhost$
^127\.
^0\.0\.0\.0$
^10\.
^172\.(1[6-9]|2[0-9]|3[01])\.
^192\.168\.
^169\.254\.
^metadata\.google\.internal$
^fd[0-9a-f]{2}:
^fe80:
^::1$
